/target

# Real, sensitive personal documents used for local manual testing only.
# CLAUDE.md hard rule: never test against real user data; SPEC.md section 4
# also says calibration data must be kept outside the repo. This must never
# be committed or pushed.
/testData
/data2*

# /data is intentionally NOT ignored: it is a fully synthetic corpus
# generated by `cargo run -p xtask`, committed so CI can exercise the
# engine against it on every OS. Regenerate with xtask, never hand-edit.

# Local scratch notes for resuming a paused session; never meant to be committed.
/SESSION_STATE.md

# Log.info/Log.error output (crates/engine/src/applog.rs): hourly-rotating
# runtime diagnostics, not source - never meant to be committed.
/logs

# Ad-hoc CLI output from manually running `analyze`/`similar` against real
# personal data (CLAUDE.md hard rule: never commit real user data). Not
# source, not a reproducible fixture - regenerate against /data if needed.
/scan-cache.json
/similar-report.json
/similar-stderr.txt
